><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Swanson</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neuronal glutathione deficiency and age-dependent neurodegeneration in the EAAC1 deficient mouse</article-title><source>Nat Neurosci</source><year>2006</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>126</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16311588</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nn1609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krizman-Genda</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonzales</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Zelenaia</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence that Akt mediates plated-derived growth factor-dependent increases in activity and surface expression of the neuronal glutamate transporter, EAAC1</article-title><source>Neuro Pharmacol</source><year>2005</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>872</fpage><lpage>882</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nieoullon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Canolle</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Masmejean</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Guillet</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pisano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lortet</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The neuronal excitatory amino acid transporter EAAC1/EAAT3: does it represent a major actor at the brain excitatory synapse?</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><year>2006</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>1007</fpage><lpage>1018</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16800850</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1471-4159.2006.03978.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kiryu-Seo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gamo</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tachibana</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiyama</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Unique anti-apoptotic activity of EAAC1 in injured motor neurons</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>3411</fpage><lpage>3421</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16858406</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.emboj.7601225</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sims</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Straff</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Platelet-derived growth factor rapidly increases activity and cell surface expression of the EAAC1 subtype of glutamate transporter through activation of phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>274</volume><fpage>5228</fpage><lpage>5237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10671571</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.275.7.5228</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fournier</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonzalez</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rapid trafficking of the neuronal glutamate transporter, EAAC1</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2004</year><volume>279</volume><f